{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DISPOSITION CORRECTED. The two earlier RCA comments get the mechanism roughly right but reach the wrong conclusion -- 'host-environment artifact, no code fix warranted'. That conclusion is contradicted by this project's own recorded policy and by an existing regression oracle that this file simply escaped.\n\nClosed ticket 3476-4472-3407-4246 (embolismic-adverse-dragon) states it verbatim: 'the supported test suite must run both locally and in CI. Treat agents dismissing reproducible local test failures as environmental noise as an anti-pattern.' That ticket converted 13 files off the same construct and added tests/integration/test_bare_repository_fixture_portability_heldout.py as a held-out guard.\n\nThe guard did not catch this one because it pins a hardcoded 3-entry _FIXTURE_NODES allowlist. test_atomic_completion_close.py was added 2026-08-25 by commit 1cb1cdd25aff -- four days AFTER the guard landed and three days BEFORE 3476 closed -- reintroducing the banned construct at five sites. There is no static sweep anywhere (scripts/, Makefile, .pre-commit-config.yaml) that would flag it; scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py covers an unrelated concern.\n\nTwo factual corrections to the original report, now reflected in the retitled ticket: the refs/heads/tickets ref EXISTS and resolves fine (git refuses to open the bare repo before any ref lookup), and git 2.55.0 is irrelevant -- safe.bareRepository shipped in git 2.38.0 on 2022-10-03 with exactly these semantics, so the behavior is four years old and there is no version regression to chase.\n\nTitle and description rewritten around the actual cause. AC4 deliberately targets the allowlist itself: fixing only the five call sites would leave the same gap that produced this recurrence."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1788481235483407001,"uuid":"b1e59545-005f-4d8d-b0c3-71c46917c5f9"}